--
N5008 [expr.cast]/2, [dcl.ambig.res], [expr.unary.op]: for each prefix
operator (-, *, !, ~) followed by a parenthesized non-type name and a
binary operator that can also be read as a prefix operator, the prefix
operator applies to the parenthesized name only; `-(T) - 1' with T a
type stays a cast of -1.  g++ 13 and clang++ 18 accept the program.
Fails on the round-163 build bin52.
